{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4df","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0777b-0bfc-71c2-a449-63245f4fe13c"},"sequence":202,"recorded_at":1780531400000399,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"32f7efe8-067d-4d98-a2af-fff5c474ce56","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"32f7efe8-067d-4d98-a2af-fff5c474ce56","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"32f7efe8-067d-4d98-a2af-fff5c474ce56"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"8248dbfc-f669-4e2a-8954-7c4f147bb310"},"task_id":"8248dbfc-f669-4e2a-8954-7c4f147bb310","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"8248dbfc-f669-4e2a-8954-7c4f147bb310","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-10-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board q 'get(TASK-260830-7a0s2c) { full }' 2>&1 | head -n 200\",\n  \"description\": \"Get full task details\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"ac\\\":\\\"Production behavior demonstrates: Build deterministic fixture runners, fake clocks, crash points, protocol fuzzing, hostile strings, and platform capability skips. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\\\",\\\"assignee\\\":\\\"[implementer] developer (muse)\\\",\\\"blockedBy\\\":[\\\"TASK-260830-2ciy0s\\\"],\\\"blocks\\\":[\\\"TASK-260830-2uowwk\\\"],\\\"checklist\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Build deterministic fixture runners, fake clocks, crash points, protocol fuzzing, hostile strings, and platform capability skips\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Lint clean\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\\"done\\\":false}],\\\"children\\\":[],\\\"created\\\":\\\"2026-08-29T22:00:08Z\\\",\\\"derivedBlockedBy\\\":[],\\\"derivedBlocks\\\":[],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Build deterministic fixture runners, fake clocks, crash points, protocol fuzzing, hostile strings, and platform capability skips. This is an implementation deliverable, not a specification rewrite.\\\",\\\"estimate\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"estimated\\\",\\\"scale\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fibonacci\\\",\\\"number\\\":8}},\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-7a0s2c\\\",\\\"integrationCheckpointed\\\":false,\\\"isAdvisoryBlocked\\\":false,\\\"isBlocked\\\":false,\\\"name\\\":\\\"build-fixture-fuzz-and-fault-test-infrastructure\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"spawn workload selection: class=implementation source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=muse/muse-spark/xhigh pair_source=explicit match=not_recommended snapshot=sha256:08c5d671a0c9e2350b1b8c97c08841f378392d0f4ac8edf05ecf155d29ae97bb rationale=\\\\\\\"implementation class rank 1; second leaf, the test instrument itself\\\\\\\"\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: muse via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[muse,claude], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\\\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=muse; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\\\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260906-d06074, max_parallel=20)\\\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260906-d06074)\\\",\\\"observability\\\":{\\\"readiness\\\":{\\\"advisoryBlockedElementIds\\\":[],\\\"blockedElementIds\\\":[],\\\"coverage\\\":{\\\"complete\\\":true,\\\"estimated\\\":1,\\\"ratio\\\":\\\"1/1\\\",\\\"total\\\":1,\\\"unestimated\\\":0},\\\"estimateKind\\\":\\\"estimated\\\",\\\"isAdvisoryBlocked\\\":false,\\\"isBlocked\\\":false,\\\"rolledEstimate\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"estimated\\\",\\\"scale\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fibonacci\\\",\\\"number\\\":8}}},\\\"scope\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-7a0s2c\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"build-fixture-fuzz-and-fault-test-infrastructure\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"task\\\"},\\\"summary\\\":{\\\"active\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830