  variable is a legitimate absence, while a failed read must never\n40|//     masquerade as one, so lookup reports only what it read.\n41|//   - literals carries explicit key=value pairs (workspace-derived values,\n42|//     SpawnPlan literals). Keys must satisfy IsEnvName and must be disjoint\n43|//     from allowed: a literal that shadows an inherited name would make the\n44|//     child's environment depend on map order rather than on policy.\n45|//   - values must be NUL-free valid UTF-8. Empty values are admitted:\n46|//     FOO= is a meaningful empty assignment, not a missing one.\n47|//\n48|// The result is sorted by name and rendered k=v, so identical inputs build\n49|// byte-identical environments. lookup abstracts the parent environment for\n50|// tests; production passes os.LookupEnv.\n51|//\n52|// No length bound is enforced here: the Section 5.1 literal bounds apply\n53|// to the SpawnPlan wire object in internal/provhost. No default allowlist\n54|// is declared here either: with no provider implementation in this\n55|// repository to derive runtime needs from, a baked-in list would be an\n56|// invented product policy, so the operator supplies the list explicitly\n57|// and ExecRunner inherits the parent environment until one is supplied.\n58|func BuildEnv(allowed []string, literals map[string]string, lookup func(string) (string, bool)) ([]string, error) {\n59|\tif lookup == nil {\n60|\t\treturn nil, failEnv(\"env lookup missing\", \"no parent environment reader\")\n61|\t}\n62|\tseen := make(map[string]bool, len(allowed))\n63|\tfor _, name := range allowed {\n64|\t\tif !IsEnvName(name) {\n65|\t\t\treturn nil, failEnv(\"env name\", name)\n66|\t\t}\n67|\t\tif seen[name] {\n68|\t\t\treturn nil, failEnv(\"env allowlist duplicate\", name)\n69|\t\t}\n70|\t\tseen[name] = true\n71|\t}\n72|\tfor key := range literals {\n73|\t\tif !IsEnvName(key) {\n74|\t\t\treturn nil, failEnv(\"env name\", key)\n75|\t\t}\n76|\t\tif seen[key] {\n77|\t\t\treturn nil, failEnv(\"env literal collision\", key)\n78|\t\t}\n79|\t}\n80|\tvalues := make(map[string]string, len(allowed)+len(literals))\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
