{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d2fb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0777b-0bfc-71c2-a449-63245f4fe13c"},"sequence":2008,"recorded_at":1780531400004011,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"32f7efe8-067d-4d98-a2af-fff5c474ce56","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"32f7efe8-067d-4d98-a2af-fff5c474ce56","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"32f7efe8-067d-4d98-a2af-fff5c474ce56"},"call_id":"call_01a07789c9037c32887254d1b899f920","text":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(594 line(s) above)\n595|`ModeIrregular` for the default arm (junctions, mount points,\n596|AppExecLinks, cloud placeholders) are both refused, with two stated\n597|counterexamples to any universal claim — `AF_UNIX` surfaces as\n598|`ModeSocket` (refused later by the regular-target gate) and `DEDUP`\n599|carries no type bit (regular by design), neither escape-capable. The\n600|package mutates no durable state and keeps no cache, so it has no\n601|crash or idempotency surface.\n602|\n603|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n604|\n605|```bash\n606|go test ./internal/secprim -count=1\n607|go test ./internal/secprim -cover -count=1\n608|```\n609|\n610|## Canonical JSON and Immutable Object Identities\n611|\n612|[`internal/canonicaljson`](internal/canonicaljson) exposes the production RFC\n613|8785 JCS entry point and the AX immutable-object identity calculation. The JCS\n614|path validates I-JSON input before canonicalization, including duplicate-name,\n615|UTF-8, surrogate-pair, ECMAScript number-formatting, string-escaping, and\n616|UTF-16 property-ordering rules. Its number behavior is checked against every\n617|finite RFC 8785 Appendix B sample through the production entry point.\n618|\n619|All four Section 1.6 boundary fixtures that publish a digest are pinned:\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
