uint53/sorted-strings-halves/Fault rendering, both leaves' arm censuses derive the bridge from environ source.\\n- FINDING (B2): witness `\\\\\\\\ud800\\\\udc00` (escaped backslash + literal ud800 + real lone low) admitted by sessadapter.DecodeTuple (Version rewritten to `\\\\\\\\ud800`+U+FFFD) and dirnode.CheckScanRequest while environ/canonicaljson/provhost refused — the raw scan misread quoted text as a high surrogate and paired it with the following real escape. Closed by delegation, not by widening the scan. All five judges refuse post-fix (probe logs kept).\\n- FINDING (corpus one-sidedness): frameCorpus sampled backslash-run parity but never an even run WITH a following real escape — green over the hole. The corpus now proves both directions: run-parity rows (over-strict side, verdicts flipped to member arms with frame phrase absent) plus even-run-plus-real-escape compositions (admit-hole side).\\n- FINDING (B1): live-planted all 7 reviewer shapes into internal/provider — old name census caught 2/7 (ledgered-name func/method); new name+shape census catches 7/7 plus a fresh-name grammar copy (evidence log kept). Shape census also surfaced 5 canonicaljson rune measures and scalar's third-spelling raw-scan gate that the name census never saw; scalar/provhost/canonicaljson copies ledgered as unification residue in TASK-260906-33xcnc.\\n- FINDING (F1/F2): environ had zero production callers and 6 functions at 0%; now DecodeStrictObject/HasLoneSurrogateEscape are called from both facades, coverage 76.1%→89.8%, no function at 0%. Denominator re-derived from production: 31 refuse arms + 58 boolean exits = 89. Battery: 27 applied / 27 killed (26 narrowing + token-preserving T1 with census green and 7 behavioral rows reddening); 22 of 89 exits directly killed, 67 residue stated by function.\\n- FINDING (new, fixed): environ.rawUint53 admitted `12a` as 12 (Decoder reads one value and stops); covered by new M4 mutant + trailing check. Sibling sessadapter/dirnode/provhost