ashes (`\\\\\\\\\\\\ud800`) are a real lone escape (odd runs escape, even runs quote), not divergence; row corrected to all-refuse before green.\\n- EVIDENCE: attached TASK-260830-3bkz0c_boundary.md (7/7 AC rows with call sites) + TASK-260830-3bkz0c_mutation-log.md. Narrowing mutants 6/6 killed (N1/N2/N3/N4/N6 + token-preserving T1 raw-scan rewrite with census still green); D1 delete-only killed, scored as existence only. Tree sha-verified identical post-battery.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (19 pkgs), environ `-race` exit 0, cover 76.1%, `go vet ./...` + `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (unchanged), catalog generate no-diff, `go build ./...` exit 0.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off with CR published (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 1035 — Directory-node leaf round-2 rework: rev1 B1/B2/B3 closed, 185-mutant battery\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-ljkj8r round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev1, changes requested, B1–B3 blocking). Test-only additions inside `internal/dirnode/` (`bound_census_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `query_operations_test.go`, `arm_identity_test.go`) plus four one-line fixture-surgery fixes (`query_test.go` unknown_field + missing caller, `manifest_test.go` missing member, `probe_test.go` missing member) and three edge extensions (findings 4097, cursor 1/1024 admission, projection bound edges). No production behavior change. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (B1): bound census ported from the sessadapter leaf — 101 production-derived sites (9 helpers + len/length-var guards, 10-shape space with 6 derived + 4 stated), 72 driven + 29 exempt mechanism/plumbing. Edge drivers prove min-1/min/max/max+1 through the production entry. Battery: 185 applied / 142 behavioural kills / 43 equivalent-with-bound / 0 survivors, zero not-applied, zero compile failures. Census-only kills scored separately (2 live census mutants + 3 synthetic gate proofs).\\n- FIX (B2): `TestDecodeQueryAllOperationsAdmit` drives 17/17 registry operations (was 5/17); 40+ validator defects through DecodeQuery including the review probes environments/\\\"root\\\", jobs/\\\"pwned\\\", distinct/\\\"secret\\\" (battery V01–V03, all killed). Zero functions at 0.0% (was 10, all §10.8.5 validators).\\n- FIX (B3): unknown_field rebuilt without the duplicate member + reachability proof; audit found the same rename-instead-of-delete slide in three more missing vectors, all fixed to deletions + message-identity proof. Protocol relabeled-major placeholder verified genuine (overridden with a real relabeled frame).\\n- FINDINGS: (1) Closed vocabularies mask bound narrowings — 11 count ceilings equal their vocabulary size (no ceiling+1 member buildable) and 20 element bounds cannot discriminate behind the outer gate; all recorded as equivalents, never survivors. (2) Count/index gates coincide at the 65th operation — each single weakening is masked behind the other; pinned jointly. (3) Test scaffolds must not size probes from production constants: the frame suite initially referenced MaxFrameBytes and went green under a widened constant; now retyped (frameBoundBytes) like all fixtures. Same fix applied to two protocol oversize vectors and the uint53 ceiling probe.\\n- EVIDENCE: attached TASK-260830-ljkj8r_round2.md (verdicts, equivalence classes, full 185-row table, 9/9 AC mapping). Production files byte-identical (battery is copy-back per mutant; post-run grep for mutant literals clean).\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (18 pkgs), `-race` on dirnode exit 0, `go vet ./...` and `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=94, unchanged). Dirnode cover 74.9% → 83.3%.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n### 0930 — Directory-node leaf: `internal/dirnode` implemented with enumerated census first\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-ljkj8r (second leaf of STORY-260830-3drr2m). New package `internal/dirnode`: two-major manifest bootstrap, envelope framing, manifest/probe/scan/Directory-Query framing, façade host checks, Structured Error 1.2.0 refusals. Six traceability rows (88 → 94), README paragraph. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- CENSUS FIRST: the leaf-1 lesson (seven rounds, one repeating mistake class) is applied before the battery, not after. `census_test.go` enumerates 10 of 10 AST shapes carrying an error construction (literal, binary-expr with rendered key, constructor registration, New-outside-body, New-as-value, ctor alias in every position, closure-hidden call, aliased import, frameFault literal) with synthetic proofs and named residue. Result: 147 derived arms (145 witnessed + 2 defensive), 8 constructors. The census caught 5 missing witness rows and 3 vacuous fixture vectors during authoring.\\n- NO-OP-PROOF VECTORS: every fixture-surgery site uses `replaceOnce`, which fails when the needle is absent — a mutation that changes nothing can no longer pass against a still-valid body.\\n- FINDINGS: (1) §10.8.5 prose names `query_cursor_mismatch` but the pinned error registry does not register it — cursor reuse refuses as `query_invalid` with a cursor-mismatch detail. (2) The response envelope carries its own `schema` + `schema_version` (1.0.0 both majors): the downgrade tuple names a response schema_version no schemaless reading can carry. (3) `node manifest is not canonical JSON` is reachable, not defensive: extensions values cross opaquely while the canonicalizer enforces depth 256 (300-deep vector proves it). (4) `failCapability` removed — no entry point in this deliverable raises `capability_unavailable`; the taxonomy test pins the 8 emitted codes instead of keeping a dead constructor for census symmetry.\\n- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery M1–M8, all killed, 0 survivors (M1 downgrade-retryable, M2 v1-macos, M3 conditional-upgrade, M4 scan-replay, M5 index-contiguity, M6 relabeled-schema-version, M7 reasonless-capability, M8 aliased-import with full behavioral suite green). Every mutant copy-aside/copy-back with `cmp` clean; exit codes unpiped. Census-only kills (M8's 4) scored separately.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (18 pkgs), `-count=3` and `-race` on dirnode exit 0, `-race` on traceability+tracecheck exit 0, `go vet ./...` and `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=94). Full-repo `-race` not run (exceeds one bounded call; raced every touched package instead). Dirnode cover 75.0%.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n### 0618 — Session-adapter leaf round-4 rework: rev3 B4/B5/B6 closed as classes, N6 fixed in code\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2z3se0 round-4 rework (review-verdict-rev3, changes requested, B4–B6 blocking + N6). Test-only additions inside `internal/sessadapter/` (`zero_absent_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `import_census_test.go`) plus a two-line production-test fix in `inventory_test.go` and this entry. No production behavior change; the 323-arm inventory floor is untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n...\\n LOGBOOK.md |   9 ++++\\n README.md  | 152 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\\n 2 files changed, 161 insertions(+)\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 14321,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 3581,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
