{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d3f3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0777b-0bfc-71c2-a449-63245f4fe13c"},"sequence":2132,"recorded_at":1780531400004259,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"32f7efe8-067d-4d98-a2af-fff5c474ce56","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"32f7efe8-067d-4d98-a2af-fff5c474ce56","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"32f7efe8-067d-4d98-a2af-fff5c474ce56"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"630c5901-df2e-483e-b5fc-799336ea760c"},"task_id":"630c5901-df2e-483e-b5fc-799336ea760c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"630c5901-df2e-483e-b5fc-799336ea760c","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-75-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git diff HEAD -- README.md LOGBOOK.md task-board.config.json | head -n 120\",\n  \"description\": \"Review tracked-file delta vs HEAD\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"diff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex 17d2025..c106d81 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -5,6 +5,14 @@\\n \\n ## 2026-09-06\\n \\n+### 2035 — secconftest instrument leaf: runners, fake clocks, crash points, fuzz, hostile strings, skips\\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-7a0s2c (second leaf of STORY-260830-1i3qu7). New package `internal/secconftest` (doc/runner/clock/crash/fuzz/hostile/skip + 6 test files): sorted deterministic Runner with execution digest and zero-call refusal, wall-clock-free Fake with Recording wiring detector, CR-MAT-* Injector over a three-phase Transactor with §13.13 outcomes and idempotency_mismatch, 8 Fuzz targets through one shared Driver with seed arrival proofs, 18-class spec-derived hostile roster plus symlink-escape commit witness, 4 probed capabilities with strict-platform failure. Leaf-1 `internal/secprim` production untouched; `task-board.config.json` gains the 8 required fuzz validation commands (pinned by `TestConfiguredValidationRunsEveryFuzzTargetWithFixedBudget`, which failed until registered).\\n+- FINDING: the repo already forces fuzz registration — a new Fuzz target without a config line fails `TestConfiguredValidationRunsEveryFuzzTargetWithFixedBudget` plus its coverage parent. The instrument therefore cannot silently add unfuzzed-in-CI targets.\\n+- FINDING (M6): a Fake leaking `time.Now` is caught by two fresh fakes disagreeing (real timestamps in the failure), not just by the sleep test — the stronger kill.\\n+- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-7a0s2c_secconftest.md` (6/6 AC rows with call sites, 10-row mutant table: 4 narrowing + 4 arm-deletion + 2 census-only, 10/10 killed, 0 survivors; M4 token-preserving mutant with 222-pass/1-fail full-suite run; darwin skip report skipped=0; digest `5569f34caab734eb` x3).\\n+- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (21 pkgs), `-race` exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (secconftest 86.9%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (94 cases, unchanged). 8/8 fuzz targets pass 5s smoke and `-fuzztime=100x` with no corpus written.\\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n+\\n ### 1939 — secprim round-3 rework: C1 handle binding, C2 classify-before-close, C3 spelling bound, N24 restored\\n - SCOPE: TASK-260830-2ciy0s round-3 (review-verdict-rev2, C1–C4 blocking). Production: `internal/secprim/nofollow.go` (`guardRootMatches` fstat dev/ino compare via `os.SameFile`, new `guard root mismatch` site in `Guard.Open`); `open_member_unix.go` (classify-before-close at both sites); spelling bound stated in `errors.go`/`inventory_test.go`/README + `TestRefusalInventorySpellingBoundIsStated`; honest reparse mapping in both windows files + README. Tests: `guard_root_test.go` (foreign-handle refusal + matched control, cross-platform), depth-3/4 full-string vectors in `open_unix_test.go`.\\n - ROOT CAUSE (C1): `openCommitRelative(root, _ string, ...)` discarded `guard.root`; unix walked the handle, Windows the path — one entry, two containment roots. Fixed in shared `Guard.Open` so both answer identically.\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex 6026a8b..4c59dc6 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -607,6 +607,59 @@ go test ./internal/secprim -count=1\\n go test ./internal/secprim -cover -count=1\\n ```\\n \\n+## Security Conformance Test Instrument\\n+\\n+[`internal/secconftest`](internal/secconftest) is the test instrument\\n+for the Section 16 production gates above: deterministic fixture\\n+runners, fake clocks, crash points, protocol fuzz drivers, hostile\\n+strings, and platform capability skips. It decides nothing itself —\\n+every refusal stays in `secprim`, every grammar in\\n+[`internal/scalar`](internal/scalar), every bound check in\\n+[`internal/environ`](internal/environ) — and every mechanism ships\\n+with a proof that disabling it reddens the suite.\\n+\\n+The `Runner` executes named fixtures in sorted order over an explicit\\n+seed and folds names, reports, and production-call counts into one\\n+digest; a fixture that records no production call is refused, so a\\n+corpus that never reaches the entry point cannot pass as coverage.\\n+`Fake` is a manually advanced clock that never reads the wall clock\\n+(a 20 ms sleep moves `time.Now` and not the fake), and the `Recording`\\n+wrapper makes an unwired clock read as zero calls — detected, not\\n+passed. The `Injector` arms named `CR-MAT-*` crash points over a\\n+three-phase durable-commit model with the Section 13.13 outcome\\n+vocabulary (`safe_retry`, `explicit_rollback`,\\n+`recoverable_parked_state`); identical retries return the\\n+byte-identical receipt while a changed body fails with\\n+`idempotency_mismatch` and stages nothing new. Eight `Fuzz*` targets\\n+drive the argv, member-path, env-name, redact, escape, render,\\n+guard-resolve, and case-collision entries through one shared `Driver`\\n+that seed-corpus tests prove reaches production (22 arrivals per\\n+entry), and every target is registered in the configured validation\\n+matrix. The hostile roster derives 18 classes from the pinned\\n+specification text (every quote verified in its section) with members\\n+generated from Unicode tables and `scalar` predicates rather than the\\n+gates under test, plus a symlink-escape commit witness gated on a\\n+probed capability. Capability probes (`symlink`, `fifo`,\\n+`mode-bits`, `nonroot`) skip only where the platform cannot provide\\n+and fail on strict platforms where absence is unexpected; on\\n+darwin/arm64 all four hold and the suite reports `skipped=0`.\\n+\\n+Run the focused tests, race, coverage, and fuzz smoke with:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./internal/secconftest -count=1\\n+go test ./internal/secconftest -race -count=1\\n+go test ./internal/secconftest -cover -count=1\\n+go test ./internal/secconftest -run='^$' -fuzz='^FuzzCheckArgv$' -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\n+```\\n+\\n+Stated bounds: the commit model proves the injector and the outcome\\n+vocabulary, not any product recovery path; fuzz covers the Section 16\\n+string and vector gates, not containment races; tombstone-deletion and\\n+TOCTOU shapes have no product surface in this story and are not\\n+driven. No new capability is advertised: the instrument cannot enable\\n+a platform lane or provider suite.\\n+\\n ## Canonical JSON and Immutable Object Identities\\n \\n [`internal/canonicaljson`](internal/canonicaljson) exposes the production RFC\\ndiff --git a/task-board.config.json b/task-board.config.json\\nindex 192bea9..4e32dce 100644\\n--- a/task-board.config.json\\n+++ b/task-board.config.json\\n@@ -256,6 +256,14 @@\\n           \\\"go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzObjectIdentityRepresentationInvariant$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n           \\\"go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzClosedIdentityShapeRefusal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n           \\\"go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzObservationEventRefusal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n+          \\\"go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzCheckArgv$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n+          \\\"go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzCheckMemberPath$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n+          \\\"go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzIsEnvName$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n+          \\\"go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzRedactCorpus$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n+          \\\"go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzEscapeForTerminal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n+          \\\"go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzRenderForTerminal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n+          \\\"go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzGuardResolve$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n+          \\\"go test ./internal/secconftest -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzDetectCaseCollision$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n           \\\"go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\\\",\\n           \\\"go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.5.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.5.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\\",\\n           \\\"GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...\\\",\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8045,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2012,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
